<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Comparison of the proposed policy with related work categories across key properties: ambiguity-aware (AA), asymmetric costs (AC), inference-time learning (ITL), and dataset &amp; model agnostic (DMA).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the following sections, we present the problem setup, theoretical results for calibrated models, the proposed algorithm with regret analysis, and experimental evaluation. Proofs are in the appendix; additional results and details are in the supplementary material.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Problem Setting</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider a system consisting of an edge device and an edge server. The device needs to infer relevant information from each sample arriving periodically, which is then used to make control decisions.
This work focuses on the case where this inference task is a cost-sensitive binary classification or event detection.
The system is equipped with two DL models trained for this task: a local DL (LDL) deployed on the device, and a remote DL (RDL) deployed on the server.
Given the memory and computing constraints of the device, the LDL is lightweight and, therefore, has lower accuracy than the RDL.
We focus on the HI framework, where each sample is first processed by the LD. Based on its output, the system either makes a local inference or offloads the sample to the RDL for better inference.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Inference Task</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume samples <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> arrive i.i.d. in time slots indexed by <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
The goal of the classifier is to map each sample to one of two possible classes, <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
To this end, the model outputs a softmax tuple <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f_{0}(x_{t}),f_{1}(x_{t}))\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f_{0}(x_{t}),f_{1}(x_{t}))\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\!\leq\!f_{0}(x_{t}),\!f_{1}(x_{t})\!\leq\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>,</mo></mpadded><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\!\leq\!f_{0}(x_{t}),\!f_{1}(x_{t})\!\leq\!1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}(x_{t})\!+\!f_{1}(x_{t})\!=\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}(x_{t})\!+\!f_{1}(x_{t})\!=\!1</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the remainder of this work, we define the class <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> as the class or event of interest and <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}\coloneq f_{1}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}\coloneq f_{1}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> as the corresponding LDL output. We assume that the model outputs are expressed using <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> bits and therefore are quantized into <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{b}</annotation></semantics></math> values. This is true for any practical system and has also been assumed in related literature.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Loss Function</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We denote the LDL and RDL models by the binary classifiers <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{l}(.)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}(.)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="h_{r}(.)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{r}(.)</annotation></semantics></math>. For each sample <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we either use <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> or offload the sample and use <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{r}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{r}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> as our inference.
In the absence of knowledge of the ground truth class for each sample, we treat the inference of the RDL as a proxy for this ground truth. This is justified by the fact that in any non-trivial scenario, the LDL aims to achieve the performance of the RDL, and no more.
Under this consideration, we have two types of classification errors that can occur when the inference is made locally:</p>
<ol id="S2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">False-positive (FP), when, <math id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l}(x_{t})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}(x_{t})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{r}(x_{t})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{r}(x_{t})=0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">False-negative (FN), when, <math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l}(x_{t})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}(x_{t})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{r}(x_{t})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{r}(x_{t})=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1},\delta_{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1},\delta_{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the normalized false positive, false negative, and offload cost at time <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\!&lt;\!\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">&lt;</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\!&lt;\!\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by an oblivious adversary.
Normalization is done by subtracting the common LDL processing cost and scaling by the maximum cost, mapping all values to <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
When a local inference is made, the system incurs a loss of <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi_{t}=\begin{cases}\delta_{1}&amp;\text{if FP}\\
\delta_{-1}&amp;\text{if FN}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>if FP</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>if FN</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi_{t}=\begin{cases}\delta_{1}&amp;\text{if FP}\\
\delta_{-1}&amp;\text{if FN}\\
0&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We assume that <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is presented to the policy at the start of round <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. The system is trivial when <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\!\geq\!\max\{\delta_{1},\delta_{-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\!\geq\!\max\{\delta_{1},\delta_{-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, enabling an assumption of <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\!\leq\!\beta\!=\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\!\leq\!\beta\!=\!1</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
Let <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> denote the policy (or algorithm) making offloading decisions and <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{t}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{t}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the incurred cost at round <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle l_{t}(\pi)=\begin{cases}\phi_{t}&amp;\text{if $h_{l}(x_{t})$ is used}\\
\beta_{t}&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">if </mtext><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> is used</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">otherwise</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle l_{t}(\pi)=\begin{cases}\phi_{t}&amp;\text{if $h_{l}(x_{t})$ is used}\\
\beta_{t}&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The corresponding cumulative loss <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{T}(\pi)\!=\!\sum_{t=1}^{T}l_{t}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.0539em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.0539em" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{T}(\pi)\!=\!\sum_{t=1}^{T}l_{t}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>. In the remainder of this work, we omit <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and refer to these as <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, for simplicity.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Threshold-based Policies and Performance Metric</h3>

<div id="S2.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Recall that for each sample, LDL outputs a score </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> corresponding to class </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. It follows that if </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is large (close to 1) or small (close to 0), it is very likely that the ground truth is 1 or 0.
On the other hand, intermediate values of </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> imply ambiguity.
Motivated by this, we focus on threshold-based HI policies where the offloading decision in each slot </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is governed by a tuple </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\theta}\coloneq(\theta_{l},\theta_{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≔</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\theta}\coloneq(\theta_{l},\theta_{u})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\!\leq\!\theta_{l}\!\leq\!\theta_{u}\!\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\!\leq\!\theta_{l}\!\leq\!\theta_{u}\!\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. A sample is offloaded if </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{l}\!\leq\!f_{t}\!&lt;\!\theta_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{l}\!\leq\!f_{t}\!&lt;\!\theta_{u}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, predicted as class </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> if </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}\!\geq\!\theta_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">≥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}\!\geq\!\theta_{u}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and class </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> otherwise.
Our goal in this work is to learn these thresholds online.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We say that a policy is a fixed-threshold (fixed-</span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) policy if </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> does not change over the time-horizon of interest.
For simplicity, we overload the notation </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> from (</span><a href="#S2.E2" title="In Loss Function ‣ 2 Problem Setting ‣ Inference Offloading for Cost-Sensitive Binary Classification at the Edge" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) and reuse it to denote </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{t}(\vec{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{t}(\vec{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}(\vec{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}(\vec{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, the instantaneous and cumulative losses incurred, respectively, by a fixed-threshold policy that uses </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as the threshold tuple.
It follows that</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle l_{t}(\vec{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle l_{t}(\vec{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\beta_{t}&amp;\text{if }\theta_{l}\leq f_{t}&lt;\theta_{u},\\
\phi_{t}&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\beta_{t}&amp;\text{if }\theta_{l}\leq f_{t}&lt;\theta_{u},\\
\phi_{t}&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SSx1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Define </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\theta}^{*}\!=\!(\theta_{l}^{*},\theta_{u}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\theta}^{*}\!=\!(\theta_{l}^{*},\theta_{u}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as the thresholds with the lowest expected cumulative loss in the class of fixed-</span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> policies.</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vec{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vec{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\arg\min_{\vec{\theta}}\mathbb{E}\left[L_{T}(\vec{\theta})\right]=\arg\min_{\vec{\theta}}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}l_{t}(\vec{\theta})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\arg\min_{\vec{\theta}}\mathbb{E}\left[L_{T}(\vec{\theta})\right]=\arg\min_{\vec{\theta}}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T}l_{t}(\vec{\theta})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SSx1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Unless otherwise mentioned, </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[.]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[.]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denotes expectation taken over the randomness in the arrival sequence and that in the candidate policy. We use a fixed threshold policy with threshold as </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\theta}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\theta}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as the baseline to compare the performance of candidate policies. Our performance metric for a candidate policy is regret, denoted by </span><math id="S2.SSx1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SSx1.p2.3.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[L_{T}]-\mathbb{E}[L_{T}(\vec{\theta}^{*})]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[L_{T}]-\mathbb{E}[L_{T}(\vec{\theta}^{*})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Optimal Policy Under a Calibrated Model</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In this section, we focus on the setting where the LDL is calibrated, i.e., for each sample, the LDL output (softmax value) for each class is equal to the a posteriori probabilities of that sample belonging to that class.
Let </span><math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cal{X}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denote the input space and the label space, respectively.
Assume that </span><math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{t},h_{r}(x_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{t},h_{r}(x_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is drawn i.i.d from </span><math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cal{X}\times\cal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒳</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cal{X}\times\cal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Calibrated Model)<span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The DL model that generates the softmax values <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-f_{t},f_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-f_{t},f_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> for the sample <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is calibrated, if
<math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(h_{r}(x_{t})=1|x_{t})=f_{t},\,\forall t." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(h_{r}(x_{t})=1|x_{t})=f_{t},\,\forall t.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We now characterize the optimal HI offloading policy for cost-sensitive classification for calibrated LDL.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the sample input to a calibrated LDL. Then, the optimal predictor <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{l}^{*}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{l}^{*}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{l}^{*}(x_{t})=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }f_{t}\geq\tfrac{\delta_{1}}{\delta_{1}+\delta_{-1}},\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">otherwise</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{l}^{*}(x_{t})=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }f_{t}\geq\tfrac{\delta_{1}}{\delta_{1}+\delta_{-1}},\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Further, the optimum offloading decision for this setup is to offload the sample when</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\theta_{l}^{*}}^{(t)}\coloneq\tfrac{\beta_{t}}{\delta_{-1}}\leq f_{t}&lt;1-\tfrac{\beta_{t}}{\delta_{1}}\coloneq{\theta_{u}^{*}}^{(t)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≔</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≔</mo><mmultiscripts><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\theta_{l}^{*}}^{(t)}\coloneq\tfrac{\beta_{t}}{\delta_{-1}}\leq f_{t}&lt;1-\tfrac{\beta_{t}}{\delta_{1}}\coloneq{\theta_{u}^{*}}^{(t)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">with an associated expected cost of</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[l_{t}]=\min\{\beta_{t},\delta_{1}(1-f_{t}),\delta_{-1}f_{t}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[l_{t}]=\min\{\beta_{t},\delta_{1}(1-f_{t}),\delta_{-1}f_{t}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Optimal Policy Under a Calibrated Model ‣ Inference Offloading for Cost-Sensitive Binary Classification at the Edge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> implies the following:
(i) Offloading does not occur if <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\!\geq\!\tfrac{\delta_{1}\delta_{-1}}{\delta_{1}+\delta_{-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\!\geq\!\tfrac{\delta_{1}\delta_{-1}}{\delta_{1}+\delta_{-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, half the harmonic mean of <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>;
(ii) when <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1}\!\!=\!\!\delta_{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mpadded style="width:0.716em;" width="0.716em"><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo></mpadded><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1}\!\!=\!\!\delta_{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the decision is equivalent to Chow’s rule for classification with rejection, with no offloading if <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\!\geq\!0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\!\geq\!0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and offloading if and only if <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\{f_{1}(x_{t}),f_{0}(x_{t})\}\!&lt;\!\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\{f_{1}(x_{t}),f_{0}(x_{t})\}\!&lt;\!\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. If not offloaded, the prediction is the class with the higher softmax value.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The key question is its extension to non-calibrated models, where the thresholds must be learned.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>The H2T2 Policy</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This section relaxes the assumption of a calibrated LDL, proposing instead an online policy that learns the values of the two thresholds. Any policy within our framework must make two decisions: first, whether to offload a given sample; and second, if the sample is not offloaded, the policy has to predict a class based on the LDL’s output.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Algorithm</h4>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We present the proposed HI-Hedge with Two Thresholds (H2T2) policy in Algorithm </span><a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Algorithm ‣ 4 The H2T2 Policy ‣ Inference Offloading for Cost-Sensitive Binary Classification at the Edge" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a><span id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. We note that H2T2 maps to the Prediction with Expert Advice (PEA) problem, where the </span><span id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">experts</span><span id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are the threshold tuples </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vec{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vec{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. We denote the set of experts as </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Given </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{l}\!\leq\!\theta_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{l}\!\leq\!\theta_{u}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, it follows that </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Theta|\!=\!2^{b-1}(2^{b}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Theta|\!=\!2^{b-1}(2^{b}+1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> experts.
Fig. </span><a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Algorithm ‣ 4 The H2T2 Policy ‣ Inference Offloading for Cost-Sensitive Binary Classification at the Edge" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> illustrates three regions of the experts with respect to an observed </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
We maintain weights for all experts. The probability of choosing an expert in a round is proportional to its weight in that round. This process will be discussed shortly.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> H2T2: The two threshold HI policy.</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.5" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
            <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span><span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;float:right;"><math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Input
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
